### API Reference

#### Universal Data Types

```python
from qyntara_core import QMesh, QMaterial, QScene

# QMesh - Universal mesh format
mesh = QMesh(
    vertices=np.array([[0,0,0], [1,0,0], [0,1,0]], dtype=np.float32),
    faces=np.array([[0,1,2]], dtype=np.int32),
    normals=None,  # Auto-computed
    uvs=[uv_set],  # Multiple UV sets supported
    name="MyMesh"
)

# QMaterial - PBR material
material = QMaterial(
    name="Gold",
    base_color=np.array([1.0, 0.766, 0.336], dtype=np.float32),
    metallic=1.0,
    roughness=0.1
)

# QScene - Complete scene graph
scene = QScene(
    meshes=[mesh],
    materials=[material]
)
```

#### Geometry Processing

```python
from qyntara_core.geometry import MeshProcessor

# Validate mesh
issues = MeshProcessor.validate_mesh(mesh)  # Detects n-gons, flipped normals, etc.

# Transform meshes
centered = MeshProcessor.center_mesh(mesh)
scaled = MeshProcessor.scale_mesh(mesh, scale=2.0)

# Clean topology
merged = MeshProcessor.merge_vertices(mesh, threshold=0.001)
cleaned = MeshProcessor.remove_duplicate_faces(mesh)
```

#### Format Converters

```python
from qyntara_core.io import USDConverter, GLTFConverter

# Export to OpenUSD (visionOS, Apple ecosystem)
USDConverter.export(scene, "output.usdc", binary=True)

# Export to glTF (web, Unity, Unreal)
GLTFConverter.export(scene, "output.glb", binary=True)

# Import from any format
scene = GLTFConverter.import_file("input.glb")
```

